# ─── LLM provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint works; this lab was validated
# against both OpenRouter and W&B Inference.
#
#   OpenRouter      LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
#                   LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#
#   W&B Inference   LLM_MODEL=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
#                   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.inference.wandb.ai/v1
#
# The credential is read from LLM_API_KEY. OPENROUTER_API_KEY is still accepted
# (the original skeleton used it) so an existing .env keeps working.
LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# SQLite database path (optional — defaults to ./hitl_audit.db in CWD).
# Holds BOTH the structured audit_events table and the LangGraph checkpoints.
# HITL_DB_PATH=hitl_audit.db

# GitHub username used to attribute HITL decisions in the audit trail.
# Optional: when unset, the agent resolves it once via GET /user using the token.
# GITHUB_USER=your-github-login

# GitHub Personal Access Token — REQUIRED.
#
# The agent calls the GitHub REST API directly. Generate a token at:
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens/new
# Scopes: tick `public_repo` (enough for VinUni-AI20k/PR-Demo — it's a public repo).
#
# Posting a top-level PR comment works for any authenticated user on a public repo.
# Formal reviews (Approve/Request-changes) would need collaborator status on the target.
# The agent never merges a PR.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
